# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Secrets. Nothing in this repo should need a .env, and if something starts to,
# that is worth noticing rather than gitignoring: a static site has no server to
# read one, so a secret here would be shipped to the browser.
.env
.env.*
*-service-account*.json

# Build output. `npm run build` regenerates dist/ from index.html, and CI
# rebuilds it before every deploy. Committing it only creates a second, staler
# copy of the app for the next person to be confused by.
dist/
node_modules/

# Firebase CLI local state
.firebase/
*-debug.log
firebase-export-*/

# NOT ignored, on purpose:
#
#   firebase-config.js  -- the Firebase web config is handed to every visitor
#                          anyway, and CI has no other way to build the site.
#                          Access is decided by firestore.rules.
#   backups/            -- the nightly backup workflow commits here. The repo
#                          history IS the backup; ignoring it would delete the
#                          only copy of the data that is not inside Firestore.
